{"id":5,"role":"User","content":"You are continuing the YangMills Lean 4 formalization project (goal: close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`, axiom count 6→5). Read `project_task_list` first.\n\n## Current state (session 27 → 28)\n\n**BUILD IS GREEN** (2972 jobs). All code compiles. 0 sorries, 0 new custom axioms.\n\n### What was done in session 27\n\nSession 27 implemented the FIRST CONCRETE CODING STEP for the temporal expansion approach (§8.11.32). This is documented in `docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md` §8.11.33 (appended at the end of the file).\n\n**New code added** (all 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms, verified by `#print axioms`):\n\n1. **`interfaceLinkTemporal`** (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1171) — Finset of time-0 interface links with μ=0 (temporal). These are the links INVERTED by σ.\n2. **`interfaceLinkSpatial`** (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1182) — Finset of time-0 interface links with μ≠0 (spatial). These are the links FIXED by σ.\n3. **`interfaceLinkTemporal_mem_iff`** / **`interfaceLinkSpatial_mem_iff`** — membership lemmas.\n4. **`interfaceLinkTemporal_spatial_partition`** — Disjoint + cover (L_0 = L_0_temporal ⊔ L_0_spatial).\n5. **`prod_interfaceLinkInt_eq_temporal_spatial`** — ∏_{L_0} = ∏_{temporal} · ∏_{spatial}.\n6. **`sigmaInterface_apply`** (TransferMatrix.lean:1839) — PROVES σ(U⁰)(n,μ) = U⁰(reflectSite n, μ)⁻¹ if μ=0, else U⁰(reflectSite n, μ). This formally confirms §8.11.32 Finding 1: σ inverts temporal links, keeps spatial links.\n\n### The mathematical strategy (§8.11.32-33)\n\nThe KEY INSIGHT from session 26 (§8.11.32): the reflection θ acts differently on the two types of interface links:\n- **Spatial interface links** (μ≠0): FIXED by θ — same in both f-factors.\n- **Temporal interface links** (μ=0): INVERTED by θ — ρ(w⁻¹) = ρ(w)† gives conjugation.\n\nThe NEW APPROACH: expand the test function f in the Peter-Weyl basis of TEMPORAL interface links w ONLY, keeping spatial interface links u⁰_s as parameters. This avoids the reorganization obstacle (§8.11.30-31) because:\n1. Spatial links are the same in both factors (fixed by σ).\n2. Temporal links give a Gram matrix via the triple product integral (ρ(w⁻¹) = ρ(w)† provides conjugation).\n3. The w-integral is a product of triple product integrals (PROVEN: `triple_product_character_matrix_integral`).\n\n**The Lüscher decomposition** (§8.11.33 refined strategy): After expanding f in temporal links and integrating out w:\n- The w-integral gives a Gram matrix M_{α,γ}(U⁺, u⁰_s) = ∑_δ P_δ(α)·conj(P_δ(γ))·a_δ(U⁺, u⁰_s).\n- a_δ depends on U⁺ through A_x (the product of the other 3 links in each plaquette).\n- KEY: a_δ(U⁺, u⁰_s) · exp(-β·S⁺(U⁺)/2) is part of the FULL positive Boltzmann factor exp(-β·(S⁺ + S_ts_upper)), which is PD.\n- The U⁺ integral becomes a PD kernel evaluation, and the V⁺ integral is its conjugate.\n- The product |∫ ... dμ⁺|² ≥ 0, and the sum over δ with a_δ ≥ 0 gives the result.\n\n### The clear path forward (item 79 in project_task_list)\n\n1. **Define the Peter-Weyl expansion of ψ in temporal links as a HYPOTHESIS** (finite sum). This is similar to the existing `h_char` hypothesis but for the test function instead of the Boltzmann factor. The expansion is: `ψ(U⁺, u⁰_s, w) = ∑_α c_α(U⁺, u⁰_s) · Φ_α(w)` where Φ_α = ∏_x (ρ_{λ_x}(w_x))_{i_x,j_x} are Peter-Weyl basis functions of the temporal links.\n\n2. **Substitute into the transfer matrix inner product** (using the existing Fubini infrastructure). The key identity is `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (TransferMatrix.lean:4776): ∫ G·G(θU) = ∫ g·Tg. And the transfer matrix in reflected form is `transferMatrixReflected` (TransferMatrix.lean:2299).\n\n3. **Apply `triple_product_character_matrix_integral`** (PeterWeyl.lean:1740) to evaluate the temporal link integral. The integral ∫ Φ_α(w) · conj(Φ_γ(w)) · exp(-β·S_ts_upper(w)) dw factorizes as a product over spatial sites x, each being a triple product integral ∫ χ_s · (ρ_t)_{ij} · conj((ρ_u)_{kl}) dμ.\n\n4. **Show the result is ≥ 0** using the PD property (Lüscher decomposition or `reflection_positivity_reorganization`). The key challenge: a_δ depends on U⁺, so the non-negativity requires absorbing a_δ into the PD Boltzmann factor.\n\n5. **Assemble with `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`** to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`.\n\n### Key files & line numbers\n\n**NEW (this session):**\n- `interfaceLinkTemporal` / `interfaceLinkSpatial` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1171/1182)\n- `interfaceLinkTemporal_spatial_partition` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1202)\n- `prod_interfaceLinkInt_eq_temporal_spatial` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1221)\n- `sigmaInterface_apply` (TransferMatrix.lean:1839)\n\n**EXISTING (proven in prior sessions):**\n- `triple_product_character_matrix_integral` (PeterWeyl.lean:1740) — the PROVEN triple product integral (WITH conjugation).\n- `triple_product_character_matrix_integral_timelike` (PeterWeyl.lean:2060) — WITHOUT conjugation (for spatial links).\n- `reflection_positivity_reorganization` (PeterWeyl.lean:1702) — the assembly lemma (requires Gram matrix form).\n- `multi_link_gram_psd_nonneg` (PeterWeyl.lean) — multi-link Gram matrix PSD.\n- `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` (PeterWeyl.lean:325) — PD of plaquette Boltzmann factor.\n- `plaquetteBoltzmannPD_inv` (PeterWeyl.lean:425) — PD with inverse links.\n- `interface_kernel_character_expansion` (PeterWeyl.lean:1469) — character expansion of interface Boltzmann factor.\n- `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect` (TransferMatrix.lean:5632) — the fullReflect form.\n- `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (TransferMatrix.lean:4776) — ∫ G·G(θU) = ∫ g·Tg.\n- `transferMatrixReflected` (TransferMatrix.lean:2299) — the reflected transfer matrix.\n- `sigmaInterface` (TransferMatrix.lean:1833) — σ reflection on interface configs.\n- `charFactorPos` / `charFactorInt` / `charFactorNeg` (TransferMatrix.lean:2108/2122/2136) — character factors.\n- `fourierCoeffPos` / `fourierCoeffNeg` (TransferMatrix.lean:4467/4485) — Fourier coefficients.\n- `fullReflectReindex` (TransferMatrix.lean:5376) — the w* reindexing.\n- `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:2341) — the AXIOM to close.\n- `interfaceLinkPos` / `interfaceLinkInt` / `interfaceLinkNeg` (ReflectionPositivity.lean:1093/1099/1105) — L_U/L_0/L_V partition.\n- `reflectLinkVariable` (Lattice.lean:198) — the reflection: temporal inverted, spatial fixed.\n\n### Build commands\n- Windows build: `powershell -Command \"lake build YangMills.Proofs.TransferMatrix 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\"`\n- Full build: `powershell -Command \"lake build 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\"`\n\n### Suggested first action for session 28\n1. Read §8.11.33 in the design doc for the refined proof strategy.\n2. The next major step is to define the Peter-Weyl expansion of ψ in temporal links as a HYPOTHESIS. This requires:\n   - Identifying the temporal interface links as a finite type (using `interfaceLinkTemporal`).\n   - Defining the Peter-Weyl basis functions Φ_α(w) = ∏_x (ρ_{λ_x}(w_x))_{i_x,j_x} for the product group SU(N)^{n_temporal}.\n   - Stating the expansion `ψ(U⁺, u⁰_s, w) = ∑_α c_α(U⁺, u⁰_s) · Φ_α(w)` as a hypothesis (similar to `h_char` in `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect`).\n3. Then substitute into the transfer matrix inner product and apply the triple product integral.\n4. The hardest part will be step 4 (showing ≥ 0 with U⁺-dependent a_δ). Consider whether the Lüscher decomposition (V^{1/2}·U_γ·V^{1/2}) or the `reflection_positivity_reorganization` lemma can be applied.\n5. IMPORTANT: The `charFactorInt` (product over L_0) can now be split using `prod_interfaceLinkInt_eq_temporal_spatial` into temporal and spatial parts. The temporal part provides the \"character\" in the triple product integral, and the spatial part is a spectator.\nTime: 2026-08-05 07:35:23 UTC","timestamp":1785915323,"token_count":2432,"full_token_estimate":1588,"turn":0,"is_prune_marker":false}
