{"id":8,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\docs\\transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md\n-- 2772 lines, 181302 bytes --\n 1 | # Design Document: Closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` via T = B*·B\n 2 | \n 3 | **Date**: 2026-07-30\n 4 | **Status**: Implementation (sub-steps (a)–(c), Lemma 2 sub-steps (i)–(iii), Fubini\n 5 | steps 4a–4e, and **Lemma 3 σ-inversion** DONE as of 2026-08-04 session 17\n 6 | (`fourierCoeffNeg_eq_fourierCoeffPos_fullReflect`, §8.11.25); remaining: Lemma 5\n 7 | (L² expansion reorganization) + Lemma 6 (final assembly) — see §8.11.25)\n 8 | **Goal**: Reduce axiom count from 6 to 5 by proving `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`\n 9 | from `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` + `characterOrthogonality`.\n10 | \n11 | ## 1. Overview\n12 | \n13 | The axiom `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (ReflectionPositivity.lean, line ~1366)\n14 | asserts that for `f` depending only on positive+interface links:\n15 | \n16 |     ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀ ≥ 0\n17 | \n18 | where `G = osG` is the Osterwalder-Seiler Boltzmann factor and `θ` is time-reflection.\n19 | This is equivalent (via `osG_thetaG_factorization` and `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`)\n20 | to the positivity of the transfer matrix `T`:\n21 | \n22 |     ⟨g, Tg⟩_{L²(μ⁺⁰)} ≥ 0\n23 | \n24 | The proof uses the **operator-theoretic T = B*·B argument**: the character expansion\n25 | of the interface Boltzmann factor defines an operator `B` (Fourier coefficient\n26 | extraction), and `T = B*·B` gives `⟨g, Tg⟩ = ‖Bg‖² ≥ 0`.\n27 | \n28 | ## 2. Mathematical Structure\n29 | \n30 | ### 2.1 The transfer matrix\n31 | \n32 | After the change of variables `V⁺ = reflect(U⁻)` (using\n33 | `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving` and `S⁻(U⁻) = S⁺(reflect(U⁻))`):\n34 | \n35 |     (Tg)(u) = exp(-β·S⁺(u)/2) · ∫_{V⁺} g(V⁺, σ(u⁰)) · exp(-β·(S⁺(V⁺)/2 + S_int(U⁺, u⁰, reflect(V⁺)))) dμ⁺(V⁺)\n36 | \n37 | where:\n38 | - `u = (U⁺, u⁰)` is a `PosInterfaceConfig` (positive + interface links)\n39 | - `σ` is the interface reflection: inverts time-like interface links, keeps spatial\n40 | - `S_int(U⁺, u⁰, reflect(V⁺))` is the interface action with negative part = reflect(V⁺)\n41 | \n42 | ### 2.2 The interface plaquettes\n43 | \n44 | Interface plaquettes are those NOT purely positive and NOT purely negative (i.e.,\n45 | corners straddle the time interface at signed time 0). They involve links from three\n46 | regions:\n47 | \n48 | | Type | Base site time | Directions | Links involved |\n49 | |------|---------------|------------|----------------|\n50 | | A | t=0 | (0, ν) spatial | time-0 (interface) + time-1 (positive) |\n\n... 2722 more line(s) below (use offset=51 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-05 07:36:55 UTC","timestamp":1785915415,"token_count":808,"tool_call_id":"dbc18ee6-a10c-44fa-84cf-29629d2c3948","full_token_estimate":553,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"docs/transfer_matrix_positivity_design.md","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":2772,"byte_count":181302,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":1,"is_prune_marker":false}
