aReindex_link_eq. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs).\",\"id\":\"68\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 15): PROVED Lemma 3 MAIN POINTWISE IDENTITY charFactorNeg_thetaReindex_eq_charFactorPos + star version. Uses Finset.prod_bij reindexing via reflectInterfaceLink. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs).\",\"id\":\"64\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 15): PROVED Lemma 3 sub-step 4 — Fourier coeff identity fourierCoeffNeg_thetaReindex_eq_star_fourierCoeffPos. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs).\",\"id\":\"69\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 16): PROVED thetaReindex_idempotent (θ²=θ, NOT involution) + charFactorPos/Int/fourierCoeffPos θ-invariance lemmas. KEY FINDING: θ is a PROJECTION (not bijection); sum reindexing w↦θw is INVALID. Correct reindexing is w* (swaps pos↔neg via φ, bijection iff dual is bijection). 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). See §8.11.24.\",\"id\":\"70\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 17): PROVED fullReflectReindex (w*) + per-link identity + product identity + star version + PLAIN FORM IDENTITY fourierCoeffNeg_eq_fourierCoeffPos_fullReflect (B_w = A_{w*}(σ)). KEY FINDING: σ twist requires L² expansion REGARDLESS of reindexing. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). See §8.11.25.\",\"id\":\"71\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 18): PROVED triple_product_character_matrix_integral (Step 1 of Lemma 5). 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2972 jobs).\",\"id\":\"72\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 19): PROVED gram_matrix_psd_nonneg (Step 2 of Lemma 5). 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2972 jobs).\",\"id\":\"73\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 20): PROVED multi_link_gram_psd_nonneg (Step 3 of Lemma 5). 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"74\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 21): PROVED reflection_positivity_reorganization (Step 4b of Lemma 5) + integral_matrix_element_trivial_projection. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"75\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-04 session 22): PROVED character_times_matrix_element_integral + triple_product_character_matrix_integral_timelike. Time-like triple product WITHOUT conjugation. 0 sorries, 0 NEW custom axioms. Build GREEN (2857 jobs). See §8.11.27.\",\"id\":\"77\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 23): ANALYZED character-level approach (§8.11.28) — does NOT directly work. KEY FINDINGS: (1) fullReflectReindex w* gives kernel |Φ_w⟩⟨Φ_{w*}| (NOT rank-1 same-vector), (2) σ twist breaks Mercer-PD structure (delta function δ(V⁰,σ(U⁰)) is discontinuous), (3) PD property of exp(-β·S_int) doesn't help because h factors break the quadratic form. CONCLUSION: L² expansion is NECESSARY. Documented in §8.11.29. Build unchanged (GREEN, 2857 jobs).\",\"id\":\"76\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 24): PROVED transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect (Step 1 of Lemma 5 Step 4a). Combines Step 4e + Lemma 3 to give fullReflect form: Complex.ofReal(∫ψ·Tψ) = C·∑_w F(w)·∫ Ψ_w·A_w·A_{w*}(σ) dμ⁰. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). Also did DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization challenge (§8.11.30).\",\"id\":\"78\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 25): DEEP ANALYSIS of reorganization (§8.11.31). KEY FINDINGS: (1) Reorganization CANNOT be done term-by-term — requires sum over w. (2) PD property of K alone does NOT imply ∫f(g)·f(g⁻¹)·K(g)≥0. (3) For single time-like link, per-λ integral is NOT ≥0 (inner product ⟨R,Q⟩, not norm squared). (4) Sum over σ gives Gram matrix (PSD), but full expression couples different Fourier coefficients. (5) Even/odd decomposition. (6) Non-negativity is a DEEP property requiring product structure of Boltzmann factor + support of f. (7) c^{w*}≠conj(c^w) is fundamental. MOST PROMISING ALTERNATIVE: plaquette-by-plaquette induction (approach 4).\",\"id\":\"80\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 26): KEY INSIGHT (§8.11.32) — temporal interface links are the obstacle. The reflection FIXES spatial interface links (θ(u⁰_s)=u⁰_s) but INVERTS temporal interface links (θ(w)=w⁻¹). NEW APPROACH: expand ONLY in temporal interface links w, keeping spatial interface links fixed. The w-integral is a product of triple product integrals (PROVEN), giving Gram matrix structure with a_γ≥0. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"81\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 27): DEFINED interfaceLinkTemporal/interfaceLinkSpatial (split of L_0 by μ=0 vs μ≠0) + partition lemma + product split lemma. PROVED sigmaInterface_apply (σ inverts temporal μ=0, keeps spatial μ≠0). 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2891 jobs). Refined proof strategy: Lüscher decomposition (V^{1/2}·U_γ·V^{1/2}) — a_γ depends on U⁺ through A_x, so non-negativity requires absorbing a_γ into the PD Boltzmann factor. See §8.11.33.\",\"id\":\"82\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 28): DEEP ANALYSIS of temporal expansion (§8.11.34). KEY FINDING: temporal expansion ALONE does NOT resolve the obstacle. After expanding A_w, A_{w*} in temporal-link Peter-Weyl basis and applying triple_product_character_matrix_integral, the result is c†·M·c' where c'≠conj(c) (c from A_w, c' from A_{w*}(σ) with σ twist + dual). This is NOT obviously ≥0. The c'≠conj(c) obstacle (Finding 7, §8.11.31) PERSISTS. CONCLUSION: The character-expansion approach (Steps 1-5 of Lemma 5) hits a FUNDAMENTAL obstacle. STRATEGIC PIVOT: pursue plaquette-by-plaquette induction (approach 4) as PRIMARY — matches actual Osterwalder-Seiler/Lüscher proof (confirmed by literature), avoids character expansion entirely. All needed infrastructure PROVEN: plaquetteBoltzmannPD, PositiveDefinite.prod/sum/conj, reflectPlaquetteIndex (involution), trace_plaquetteProduct_reflect_all, interface_boltzmann_eq_abstract_product. Build GREEN (unchanged, 2891 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"83\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"IN PROGRESS (STRATEGIC PIVOT): Lemma 5 via PLAQUETTE-BY-PLAQUETTE INDUCTION (approach 4). The character-expansion approach is EXHAUSTED (c†·M·c' obstacle). NEW PLAN: (1) Show ∫ G·G(θU) = ∫ [∏_p K_p(g_p)] · [∏_p K_p(θ(g_p))] where K_p = exp(c·Re Tr(plaquette_p)) is PD (plaquetteBoltzmannPD). (2) Use reflection maps plaquettes to plaquettes (reflectPlaquetteIndex involution) + PD of each factor + PositiveDefinite.prod to show the integral ≥ 0 by induction on plaquettes. (3) Assemble with integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg to close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom. See §8.11.34 for full analysis.\",\"id\":\"79\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"PENDING: Assemble lemma 6 — close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (axiom count 6→5). See §8.8. Requires Lemma 5 (item 79, now via plaquette induction).\",\"id\":\"48\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"action\":\"update\"}","name":"project_task_list"},"id":"19adfd15-4d9c-41cd-a170-9355100bc764","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":2124,"reasoning_content":"All my references are verified. The infrastructure for the plaquette induction approach exists:\n- `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` (PeterWeyl.lean:325) — PROVEN\n- `PositiveDefinite.prod` — PROVEN (used at lines 306-308)\n- `PositiveDefinite.sum` (line 75) — PROVEN\n- `PositiveDefinite.conj` (line 402) — PROVEN\n- `reflectPlaquetteIndex` / `reflectPlaquetteIndexEquiv` / `reflectPlaquetteIndex_involution` — PROVEN\n- `trace_plaquetteProduct_reflect_all` (line 2076) — PROVEN (reflection symmetry of plaquette trace)\n- `interface_boltzmann_eq_abstract_product` (line 1266) — PROVEN\n\nI'm at 66% context. Let me update the project task list with my findings and prepare the handoff. The build is unchanged (GREEN, no code changes this session — pure analysis).\n\nLet me update the project_task_list to reflect the strategic pivot to the plaquette induction approach, then handoff.","turn":52,"is_prune_marker":false}
